hi everyone i'm danny ceo and welcome to  a brand new  culinary edition of do just one thing  and today i call it why buy it when you  can diy it and what i'm talking about  are your own diy apple cider vinegar  gummies  yes you can actually make them yourself  and if you know  anything about apple cider vinegar right  now it is  all the rage and there's so many things  that people love about apple cider  vinegar the one thing that can be a  little difficult about it is that it's  not easy  to take your apple cider vinegar on the  go you imagine traveling with this  so one of my favorite things to do is to  make these really delicious  apple cider vinegar gummies because you  can take one or two or a whole bunch of  them  and enjoy your apple cider vinegar  gummies wherever  you go what you start off with  is some gelatin so what i have here is  unflavored gelatin just three packets  which equals about three tablespoons  you can find uh vegan alternatives to  gelatin too at the health food store but  you need something that's going to be  that binding agent  that makes everything into that jelly  form  that we want in our gummy bear so i just  sprinkle three of these in here and what  we want to do in this bowl  is called blooming we want the gelatin  to bloom  into a thick paste don't be scared by  the paste  it's kind of ugly but it's all going to  come together in the end and be a really  beautiful mixture that you're going to  want to chill  make beautiful gummies out of the very  next thing is you need a little bit of  lemon juice  and what i love to do is just  quarter them up just like this you can  also just squeeze them regularly but you  need about  two tablespoons of lemon juice  and what i've discovered that equals  about half a lemon  depending how juicy your lemons are  here's the last one  one of the nice things about this recipe  is that it's very forgiving so  if you have a little too much lemon  juice in there it's totally okay it's  all going to come together  and then finally because apple cider  vinegar if you've ever taken a shot  of apple cider vinegar you know it's  very pungent a little bit of sweetness  you know as you say a little bit of  sugar helps the medicine go down  well so does honey and what we're going  to do is put  three tablespoons of honey in here you  can do  an organic honey you can do a raw honey  but what i like to do is just  take whatever i have on hand  and pour this beautiful golden mixture  you only need about  five minutes of time to really put it  all together and it makes a whole bunch  of gummies which is really nice oh and  one more thing  you need water so one quarter cup of  water  to really help bring it all together now  i talked about how  blooming the gelatin will result in  something that's not so  attractive and i'll show you what you  get  it's sort of this thick gunky paste  it kind of looks like like a sugar scrub  you might use in the shower  but this is exactly what you want and  you might be thinking  we're missing something yes we're  missing apple cider vinegar so  what i've got here is half a cup of  apple cider vinegar and half a cup of  water  just bring it to a boil turn it off  we're just going to pour this all the  way on the inside  and then we're going to incorporate it  all together and you want to make sure  that the gelatin  is totally dissolved there's no clumps  in here  and as you can see in a matter of  seconds i've got my mixture  ready to go to be made  into apple cider vinegar gummies  and by the way i went online you don't  have to do this  and i bought these silicone molds in the  shape of apples  but whatever silicone mold you have is  totally fine  if you don't have a silicone mold what  you can do  is actually repurpose like an empty  juice container something with the waxy  inside  and just fill that whole thing with this  mixture  and then open it up and then cut it into  little squares and little square gummies  from that  now we're just going to fill our mulch  with the mixture one by one and just so  you guys know i have it on a plate  i learned the very hard way that if you  pour  anything into a silicone mold and it's  not on a steady surface when you try to  pick it up  you make a big hot mess in the kitchen  very quickly  and then into the refrigerator for about  30 minutes or overnight  i did one ahead of time this is what it  looks like  so you can see take this one out that it  is completely  solidified and they just pop right out  and you have a homemade apple  cider vinegar gummy and what do we say  why buy it  when you can  diy it if you're planning on making some  of these apple cider vinegar gummies  post it to your social media accounts  and be sure to tag the drew barrymore  show in your post  and don't forget we have so many recipes  and ideas and inspiration  at the drewberrymarshow.com website and  if you're even more inspired you can  find a lot more recipes in my own  magazine naturally danny seo  now on newsstands  [Music]  you
 

